The support desk merged 412 distinct reports into #4471. The exported evidence shows three independent problems, not one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Triage by tenant configuration and entry channel, then verify symptoms. Matching subject lines alone is insufficient.
</Callout>

## The separate problems

### Shared parser reads month first

[GitHub issue #1](https://github.com/przemuh/mega-dev-kb/issues/1) covers **379 reports**.
The shared date parser reads month/day when day-first tenants supply dates. App and email reports from day-first tenants, along with booking-v2 form reports, belong here.

The 5 October engineering update says this parser problem was fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Issue #1 is closed as completed.

### booking-v3 date hint conflicts with tenant locale

[GitHub issue #2](https://github.com/przemuh/mega-dev-kb/issues/2) covers **33 reports**.
booking-v3 shows an MM/DD/YYYY hint while parsing input with the tenant's day-first order. App and email reports from the same tenants remain parser reports.

The 5 October engineering update says booking-v3 was retired. Issue #2 is closed as not planned; the hint itself was not repaired.

### One-day date moves need investigation

[GitHub issue #3](https://github.com/przemuh/mega-dev-kb/issues/3) covers **5 reports**: R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, and R-41620.
Each describes a date moving by one day. A month/day swap cannot cause a one-day shift. The tenant-and-channel classifier files these reports under parser, so they remain in the historical parser count of 379, but the desk notes identify them as a separate observation.

The parser fix does not explain these reports. Keep issue #3 open while investigating original timestamps, timezone handling, date-only conversion, and the day boundary.

## Evidence

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table counts reports by the supplied classifier, after deduplicating export rows by report ID. The five one-day reports remain in the parser total for historical counting, but they require their own investigation ticket.

## Arrival time is different from merge time

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports reached the desk from April onward. The July merge spike records triage work, not the start of the incident.

## Triage consequence

<DedupeExplorer />

Identical subjects can describe different causes, and different subjects can describe the same cause. The desk must classify by tenant configuration and channel, not subject alone.

